			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Git service handlers and expand diagnostic instrumentation\n\nThree major additions to Mountain's diagnostic and service capabilities:\n\n1. **Git service handlers** (`WindServiceHandlers/Git.rs`): Implement the full `localGit` channel mirroring VS Code's `ILocalGitService` API - clone, pull, checkout, revParse, fetch, revListCount, cancel, exec, and isAvailable. Uses process PIDs for cancellation (SIGTERM on Unix, taskkill on Windows) and logs all operations under the existing `git` tag.\n\n2. **SkyEmit instrumentation** (`SkyEmit.rs`): New `LogSkyEmit` wrapper around `tauri::Emitter::emit` that logs every Mountain→Wind/Sky emit under the `sky-emit` tag. Records channel name, payload bytes, and ok/fail status. Enables traffic-volume auditing via `LAND_DEV_LOG=sky-emit`.\n\n3. **Provider registration expansion** (`MountainVinegRPCService.rs`): Extend the register_* notification handler from 8 to 34+ provider types - debug_configuration, text_document_content, folding_range, document_link, code_lens, selection_range, document_range_formatting, debug_adapter, rename, file_system, uri_handler, document_paste_edit, task, signature_help, semantic_tokens, document_highlight, workspace_symbol, on_type_formatting, inlay_hints, document_drop_edit, color, type_hierarchy, type_definition, notebook_serializer, linked_editing_range, implementation, terminal_profile, terminal_link, inline_values, inline_completion_item, file_decoration, external_uri_opener, declaration, call_hierarchy. Also extracts and logs the scheme for scheme-bound providers, and includes options in the DTO.\n\nPlus: Flexible `RenderDevLog` command now accepts both PascalCase (Tag/Message) and snake_case (tag/message) params, supporting any JS caller convention.",
			"SHA": "de6e0f842ce46f14a18508dc143e2a456644f76f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T15:57:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				776,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add RenderDevLog command and diagnostic logging tags\n\nAdd a new Tauri command `RenderDevLog` that bridges TypeScript-side tagged logs (Wind/Sky/Cocoon) into Mountain's `dev_log!` file sink. This enables a single `Mountain.dev.log` to carry the complete tag-filterable picture of a session, rather than requiring cross-referencing between browser console and log file.\n\nAlso add five new diagnostic tags to isolate architectural gaps during debugging:\n- `notif-drop`: Notifications hitting the default arm (no handler)\n- `provider-register`: Accepted register_*_provider notifications with extension IDs\n- `channel-stub`: Wind/Output TauriMainProcessService.call stub hits vs route vs miss\n- `git`: localGit channel, GitExec RPC, SCM provider group updates\n- `tree-view`: tree.register, GetTreeChildren, sky://tree-view/create events\n\nApply tags across SCM.rs, TreeView.rs, CreateEffectForRequest/TreeView.rs, and MountainVinegRPCService.rs to provide visibility into extension host integration issues.\n\nImpact: Developers can now filter `LAND_DEV_LOG=git,tree-view` to isolate specific subsystem issues, and TS-originated logs appear in the same file with `[RenderDevLog]` prefix for grep separation.",
			"SHA": "f7625f320666cca6bfe3d74fb87c4fc09444ddb3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T15:33:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				775,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Standardize Tauri event channel naming to kebab-case\n\nConsolidate all `sky://` event channel names to a consistent kebab-case format and emit TreeView registration events to the canonical path.\n\nChanges:\n- `sky://treeView/register` → `SkyEvent::TreeViewCreate` (canonical path)\n- `sky://webview/setHtml` → `sky://webview/set-html`\n- `sky://webview/postMessage` → `sky://webview/post-message`\n- `sky://status-bar/*` → `sky://statusbar/*` (remove hyphen to match family)\n- `sky://status-bar/message` → `sky://statusbar/set-message`\n\nAlso emit `SkyEvent::TreeViewCreate` after a TreeDataProvider is registered so the renderer can wire up the data provider to the matching ITreeView instance. Without this, VS Code's treeView.ts keeps `_dataProvider === undefined` and all extension tree views (GitLens, debug, SCM, tasks) render empty.\n\nThe previous diverged channel names were parallel forks that no downstream listener ever subscribed to. Impact: Extension tree views now render correctly with data from providers.",
			"SHA": "85bd2a487c73623310182363d6a35dfbe8e9c57d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
